ufs: mediatek: raise ufs_sel and the crypto clock before entering HS-G5

On boards where the core's clock scaling is off
(mediatek,ufs-clkscale-only-by-user), MediaTek moves the two UFS clocks in
only three places: its clkscale_control path, and its suspend and resume
hooks when the link sleeps or wakes at HS-G5. A power mode change from
anywhere else (the debugfs power_mode file, error recovery, the PMC after
link startup) never raises them. G5 then runs, for as long as the disk
stays awake, on whatever was left: possibly ufs_sel at 273 MHz and the
inline encryption clock (ufs_fde) at 416 MHz instead of 499.2 and 546 MHz.

Raise both, with vcore first, in ufs_mtk_pre_pwr_change() whenever the
negotiated gear is HS-G5. That runs before every PMC that goes through
ufshcd_config_pwr_mode(), including requests for the mode the link already
has, so writing the current G5 mode again also restores the fast clocks.
Nothing is lowered here: the G5 suspend hook already drops the clocks while
the disk sleeps, and lower gears work on either setting.

Against MediaTek's kernel_device_modules-6.6 (sources/mtk_vendor_6.6, the
OnePlus public copy). It builds into the MediaTek UFS vendor module, not
the kernel image.

--- a/drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c	2026-11-02 08:54:09.841208029 +0530
+++ b/drivers/ufs/ufs-mediatek.c	2026-11-02 08:54:09.859209561 +0530
@@ -1939,6 +1939,24 @@
 	if (host->max_gear == 0)
 		host->max_gear = dev_req_params->gear_rx;
 
+	/*
+	 * HS-G5 needs ufs_sel and the inline encryption clock (ufs_fde) on
+	 * their fast sources, with vcore raised first. MediaTek's own scale-up
+	 * path (ufs_mtk_config_pwr_mode()) and the G5 resume hook do this, but a
+	 * power mode change from anywhere else (debugfs, error recovery, link
+	 * startup) does not, and then G5 runs on whatever clocks were left.
+	 * Raise them here, before any PMC, so every way into G5 is covered.
+	 * Repeating it when the clocks are already fast changes nothing.
+	 * Only when the core's own clock scaling is off: otherwise devfreq
+	 * owns these clocks (same condition as the G5 suspend/resume hooks).
+	 */
+	if (!ret && !ufshcd_is_clkscaling_supported(hba) &&
+	    host->mclk.ufs_sel_clki && host->mclk.ufs_sel_max_clki &&
+	    (dev_req_params->pwr_rx == FAST_MODE ||
+	     dev_req_params->pwr_rx == FASTAUTO_MODE) &&
+	    dev_req_params->gear_rx >= UFS_HS_G5)
+		_ufs_mtk_clk_scale(hba, true);
+
 	if (ufs_mtk_pmc_via_fastauto(hba, dev_req_params)) {
 		ufs_mtk_adjust_sync_length(hba);
 
